      {
        "id": 29035,
        "name": "NDRWnerd",
        "username": "NDRWnerd",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/n/96bed5/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2012-04-28T03:30:26.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"&quot;&quot;broccoli&quot;&quot;\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n \"\"broccoli\"\":</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I think if you’ve spent a lot of time playing Absolute Zero, you’ll have a pretty good idea how heroes dealing damage to themselves in the presence of buffs works.  It really can’t work any other way without destroying his effectiveness.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Yes.  When an effect such as Galvanize increases a Heroes damage, it’s increased even when that Hero damages his- or her-self.</p>\n<p>I didn’t think so at first, but the more I read Brain Burn, the more I’m convinced each card is a seperate instance of damage.  I’ll still eagerly await an official clarifaction.  But as devestating as it can potentially be to Visionary, there’s enough ways to mitigate it. Twist the Ether, Lead from the Front + Fortitude, Smoke Bombs, Imbue Fire + Flesh of the Sun God, etc. etc.  It’s just a tricky card to use, but they’re plenty of those.</p>",
